Round-6 gpt-5.6-sol session verified the 244-action L4 prefix from two
fresh resets, then independently discovered a new counter-reset
mechanic on L5: the top-middle green-center ring is collectible by
entering horizontally from the west after a launcher places the
player at x39,y5. Pinned down the exact reason the compact
color-8-first splice fails: the third pinwheel entry leaves 10 counter
actions but the forced launcher/upper-corridor route to the
upper-left ring needs 11 -- one action short. No L5 win this round;
frontier stays at level 4 (matches registry's current 4 banked, no
regression). Next attempt should finance color 8 via the new
top-middle ring reset instead of the upper-left ring.

